{{Quote|Float like a butterfly, sting like a bee!|Nanomech.<ref name="UA">''[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]''</ref>}}
Despite being [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s smallest alien, Nanomech can still pack quite a punch. Nanomech can generate green energy from his hands and release it either as a raw discharge of electricity<ref name="AS" /><ref name="I13">''[[Inspector 13]]''</ref> or concentrated, explosive orbs of energy.<ref name="TFOWP1>''[[The Frogs of War: Part 1]]''</ref> Nanomech can also project this energy as lasers from his eyes which can destroy smaller technology, such as [[Aggregor]]'s [[Mind Control Headband]]s.<ref name="UA" />

Much like [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]], Nanomech's size allows him to squeeze into small spaces.<ref name="VG">''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]''</ref><ref name="TUH">''[[The Ultimate Heist]]''</ref> Nanomech can also reduce his size at will, even to microscopic scales.<ref name="AS" /><ref name="I13" /> He can return to his original size, but cannot grow any larger.{{Refn|[[:File:Nanomech Very Small Maximum Size.png]]|group = DJW}}

Nanomech is capable of flying, thanks to possessing a pair of wings.<ref name="UA" /><ref name="TFOWP1 />

Despite his small stature, Nanomech has enhanced strength relative to his size, as he was able to easily lift a food cover over his head.<ref name="TUH" />

Nanomech cannot be controlled by Microchip Queens; according to himself, it is because he is part [[Human (Classic)|human]], and "humans never give up". He is also resistant to electricity.<ref name="AS" /> 

Nanomech is capable of adaptation, allowing him to copy certain abilities of his opponents after being hit by their attacks, as shown when Nanomech copied the [[Decoy Queen]]'s tentacles.<ref name="AS" />

===Non-Canon Powers and Abilities===
====[[Science Friction]]====
As a form of technopathy, Nanomech's body can emit electricity to communicate with surrounding machines.

==Weaknesses==
[[File:I13 (324).png|thumb|Small Size]]
Nanomech's minuscule size can be a problem if fighting larger opponents, as he was smooshed with a spell book<ref>[[Absolute Power: Part 1|''Absolute Power: Part 1'']]</ref> and when he was incapacitated by a fly swatter.<ref name="I13" /> 

==History==
===Alien Force===
*Nanomech first appeared in '''''[[Ben 10: Alien Swarm]]''''', where he was created by the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] scanning the [[Microchip]]s and entered [[Dr. Victor Valadis|Victor]]'s brain to fight the [[Decoy Queen]]. After a grueling battle, Nanomech destroyed the Queen and thus the entirety of the chips, freeing everybody from their control.

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]'', Nanomech was used for the video game scan but was regarded as too small, so he switched into [[Jetray (Classic)|Jetray]]. Later, Nanomech disabled and defeated the [[Stalker]].
*In ''[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]'', Nanomech destroyed the headbands that were controlling [[Ra'ad]] and [[P'Andor]]. As [[Alien Force|the team]] confronted [[Aggregor]], Nanomech switched into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].
*In ''[[Absolute Power: Part 1]]'', Nanomech was squashed in [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]]'s [[Gwen's Spellbook|spellbook]], forcing him to switch into [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]].
*In ''[[Inspector 13]]'', [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] as Nanomech snuck into the [[Techadon Factory]] and was defeated by [[Thirteen]].

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]'', Nanomech briefly appeared in an accidental transformation chain before it finally ended when he switched into [[Bloxx (Classic)|Bloxx]].
*In ''[[The Frogs of War: Part 1]]'', Nanomech defeated some [[Incursean (Classic)|Incursean]]s by blowing up their guns, knocking them out.
*In ''[[The Ultimate Heist]]'', Nanomech escaped his [[Plumber Headquarters|Plumber HQ]] cell and avoided [[Blukic]] and [[Driba]] as much as possible.
*In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]'', Nanomech defeated [[Mad Ben|Mad]] Way Big.
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Nanomech appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

