==Trivia==
*Nanomech is [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s smallest alien, smaller than even [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]].<ref>''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]''</ref>
*Due to Nanomech not really being a typical alien from any sort of planet, scanning machines have trouble identifying him.
**The [[Techadon Factory]]'s computer refers to him as an "unknown biomechanical organism".<ref name="I13" />
**The [[Plumbers (Classic)|Plumbers]]' security scanners designate him an "unidentified nano-based lifeform".<ref name="TUH" />
*Along with [[Rath (Classic)|Rath]], Nanomech is [[Ashley Johnson]]'s favorite alien.{{Refn|https://youtu.be/4s8v7XQYpzs|group = AJ}}
*Throughout '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''', Nanomech was always transformed into via the quick-change feature. He was not directly transformed into by Ben in his [[Human (Classic)|human]] form.
*[[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] finds it hard to take Ben as Nanomech seriously due to his squeaky voice.<ref name="UA" /> Because of his minuscule size, Kevin also thinks Nanomech is really lame.<ref name="VG" />
*Nanomech is the only known [[Omnitrix]] alien that is part-human, as well as the only hybrid/combination transformation that can be accessed without the Omnitrix either being broken or upgraded into a [[Biomnitrix]].
*During the Birthday Bash in ''[[FusionFall]]'', players could get a Nanomech helmet modeled after his '''''[[Ben 10: Alien Swarm|Alien Swarm]]''''' design. However, after '''Ultimate Alien''' premiered, it was changed to match the animated version. This item was re-released as a code item.
*Nanomech is one of five aliens to debut in a movie or special; the others being [[Eye Guy]], [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]], [[Eon (Transformation)|Eon]], and [[Shocksquatch]].
*Nanomech is one of five aliens featured in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''' who generate green electricity; the others being [[Upgrade (Classic)|Upgrade]], [[Buzzshock (Classic)|Buzzshock]], Frankenstrike, and [[Brainstorm]].
*Nanomech's '''Ultimate Alien''' appearance was designed by [[Glenn Wong]], with color styling by Chris Hooten.{{Refn|[[:File:Nanomech by Hooten.png]]|group = GW}}
*Benchip was Nanomech's working name.{{Refn|[[:File:Nanomech Concept Art 1.png]]|group = ca}}
**Consequently, this makes Nanomech the fourth alien whose working name had Ben's name in it; the first three being [[Blitzwolfer]], [[Snare-Oh]], and [[Frankenstrike]].
**Of the four, he is the only one who neither debuted in the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' nor hailed from the [[Anur System]].
*If Nanomech had appeared in the [[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Reboot]], he would still be a hybrid rather than a different species.{{Refn|[[:File:Duncan Opinion on Nanomech.png]]|group = DR|name = duncan}}

